<Footnotes>
  <li>Before the iPad shipped, the SDK had a simulator window that ran at the device's actual pixel dimensions on your Mac. For months that 1024 by 768 rectangle was the only iPad in existence outside Cupertino. I designed the whole first version against that window.</li>
  <li>The one feature I wish we had shipped on day one is undo. The 1.0 release did not have a proper undo stack. We added it in 1.1 and support email volume dropped by half overnight.</li>
</Footnotes>
